  "authoredFrom": "Erlang type semantics + the pinned grammar's type shapes, before this fixture's F3 run. -type, -opaque and OTP 28's -nominal all declare a Type; a -callback is a Method owned by the module; every one of those bodies, plus a -spec signature and a record field type, contributes TYPE references. Two facts that only the span filter keeps apart: a declaration's OWN name is not a self-reference (so `handle` never references `handle`), while a RECURSIVE type's self-reference is legal Erlang and IS emitted (`tree :: {tree(), leaf()}` depends on itself). A record named in a type is a type REFERENCE, never a construction. UPDATED for ER-D36: a type dependency is an APPLIED name, and only an applied name. The M12 differential went 1.000 -> 0.784 with 19 false positives, two of them bare atoms in type syntax resolving to same-named types elsewhere. So `| error`, `| undefined` are atom LITERALS and declare no dependency, while `binary()`, `request()`, `reply()` are applied and stay. The three bare-atom edges this file used to REQUIRE are now FORBIDDEN with the reason attached, because a pin that can be silently deleted teaches nothing.",
